<h2 id="koppen">Climate regions and Köppen codes</h2>
<p>OpenFarm groups the world into {{ db.regions.length }} <a href="{{ '/regions/' | url }}">climate regions</a> built from the
<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K%C3%B6ppen_climate_classification">Köppen–Geiger classification</a>. A Köppen code has two or three letters:
the first is the main group (A tropical, B dry, C temperate, D continental, E polar), the second the rainfall pattern (f no dry season, s dry summer, w dry winter; for B: W desert, S steppe) and the third the summer heat (a hot, b warm, c cool, d very cold winter; for B: h hot, k cold).
Your location is looked up on a 0.5° grid (about 50 km) of the Beck et al. (2018) map, so mountains and coasts can differ from the cell.
Every code on the site links to its region; hover it to see the full name.</p>
